  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="gamiqon-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">גמיקון</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">gmyqwn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">gamiqon</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">גמיסקון</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">gmysqwn</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic">gamisqon</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <form type="inflected">
               <orth type="inflected" xml:lang="jpa">גמומסיות</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="en">gmwmsywt</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">gamomasiyot</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="num">pl.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="gamiqon-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>marriage contract</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>γαμικόν, γαμισκός</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ר' הונא בשם ר' יוסף דור המבול לא נמחו מן העולם עד שכתבו 
                     <app>
                        <lem>גמומסיות</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1">גמומוסיות</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">גממוסיות</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K">גמוסיו</rdg>
                     </app> לזכור ולבהמה</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">26,5</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 248 : 6</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">TanhB Bereʾshit 21</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">גמיקיסוס</term>); <bibl type="ancient">TanhB Bereʾshit 33</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">קמיסמסין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">LevR Aḥare 23,9</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">גומסיות</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 43</bibl></note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Sing not in GenR. The form is not sufficiently clear (corruption?). Cf. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 342b</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">AC I 311a</bibl> (<term xml:lang="ipa">גמס</term>, <term xml:lang="jpa">גמססיות</term>). <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 252a</bibl> renders sg. <term xml:lang="jpa">גמומסית</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">gmwmsyt</term> or <term xml:lang="jpa">גומסית</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">gwmsyt</term>, interpreting as “a sarcastic adaptation of <term xml:lang="jpa">γάμος</term>, to deride the hymenean songs in their licentious application to sodomy and to copulation of animals”. <bibl type="modern">Dalman 82a</bibl>: Gr. <term xml:lang="jpa">γάμος</term>. <bibl type="modern">Fürst (1890) 89b</bibl> explains as a derivative of the Gr. <term xml:lang="jpa">γαμίσκω,</term> <term xml:lang="jpa">γαμικὰ</term>.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>178b-179a</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
